course: dictionary
lesson: 9440
title: Stalactites and the clues around them
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stalactite is a long, pointed stone shape that hangs down from the roof of a cave. Its name is a clue too: the stalactite holds on to the top of the cave and points down.
explain: Read the words around it: «Stalactites hang from cave roofs and stalagmites grow up from the floor.» Hang from the roof tells you a stalactite comes down from above, and grow up from the floor tells you a stalagmite goes up from below.
explain: Water is the builder. «Drip by drip the water leaves stone behind», so the stone grows very slowly, one tiny bit at a time. To check your meaning, swap it into a sentence: a stalactite is a pointed stone hanging from a cave roof, and it still makes sense.
fact: A stalactite hangs down from the roof of a cave.
fact: A stalagmite grows up from the floor of a cave.
fact: Stalactites grow from dripping water that leaves a tiny bit of chalky mineral behind, over thousands of years.
fact: Touching a stalactite can stop it growing, because oil from your skin stops the mineral sticking.
fact: Anything hanging down in the same pointed shape, like an icicle, can also be called a stalactite.
exercise: Where do stalactites hang from? | The cave floor | A mountain top | A river bank | *The cave roof
exercise: «Drip by drip the water leaves stone behind.» What makes a stalactite grow? | *Dripping water that leaves tiny bits of mineral | Children climbing on the rocks | Hot sun baking the rock | Strong winds blowing into the cave
exercise: On a cave trip, the guide asks you not to touch the stalactites. Why? | It is rude to point at them | They might fall on you in a strong wind | *Oil from your skin can stop them growing | They are too heavy to lift
test: Which word means a stone that grows up from the cave floor? | Icicle | *Stalagmite | Stalactite | Cave roof
test: Besides a stone in a cave, what else can be called a stalactite? | A puddle on the floor | A flat sheet of rock | *An icicle hanging down in the same shape | A stalagmite growing up
exam: Which sentence explains what a stalactite is? | A stalactite is a stone that grows up from the floor | A stalactite is a hat worn by cave guides | A stalactite is a fish found in deep water | *A stalactite is a long, pointed stone that hangs down from a cave roof
